-- s 54(2) first: the definitions that s 54(1)(b) and (c) use.
-- src:581 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:582 | “local authority” means—
-- src:583 | (a) a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972 (c. 70), the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly,
-- src:584 | (b) a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994 (c. 39), or
-- src:585 | (c) a district council in Northern Ireland;
@ref s 54(2) "local authority" (src:581-585)
GIVEN `a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Common Council of the City of London` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Council of the Isles of Scilly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a district council in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(2) the body is a local authority` MEANS
    IF       `a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972`
         OR  `the Common Council of the City of London`
         OR  `the Council of the Isles of Scilly`
         OR  `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`
         OR  `a district council in Northern Ireland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“local authority” means—"

-- src:581 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:586 | “public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature.
@ref s 54(2) "public authority" (src:581-586)
GIVEN `the person or body has functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(2) the person or body is a public authority` MEANS
    IF `the person or body has functions of a public nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature"

-- src:576 | 54 Names suggesting connection with government or public authority
-- src:577 | (1) The approval of the Secretary of State is required for a company to be registered under this Act by a name that would be likely to give the impression that the company is connected with—
-- src:578 | (a) Her Majesty's Government, any part of the Scottish administration , the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland,
-- src:579 | (b) a local authority, or
-- src:580 | (c) any public authority specified for the purposes of this section by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 54(1) Names suggesting connection with government or public authority (src:576-580)
GIVEN `the name would be likely to give the impression that the company is connected with the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is Her Majesty's Government, a part of the Scottish administration, the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a local authority (s 54(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is a public authority specified for the purposes of this section by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(1) the approval of the Secretary of State is required` MEANS
    IF       `the name would be likely to give the impression that the company is connected with the body`
         AND (    `the body is Her Majesty's Government, a part of the Scottish administration, the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland`
              OR  `the body is a local authority (s 54(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR  `the body is a public authority specified for the purposes of this section by regulations made by the Secretary of State`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that would be likely to give the impression that the company is connected with" a body in (a), (b) or (c)

-- src:589 | (1) The approval of the Secretary of State is required for a company to be registered under this Act by a name that includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under this section.
@ref s 55(1) Other sensitive words or expressions (src:589-589)
GIVEN `the name includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 55` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(1) the approval of the Secretary of State is required` MEANS
    IF `the name includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 55`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations"

-- src:603 | (5) In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 56(5) "specified" (src:603-603)
GIVEN `specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(5) the department or body is specified` MEANS
    IF `specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- src:596 | (2) Where such a requirement applies, the applicant must request the specified department or other body (in writing) to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name.
@ref s 56(2) Duty to seek comments (request in writing) (src:596-596)
GIVEN `a requirement under regulations under section 54 or 55 that the applicant must seek the view of a specified Government department or other body applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(2) the applicant must request the specified department or body in writing to indicate whether and why it has any objections` MEANS
    IF `a requirement under regulations under section 54 or 55 that the applicant must seek the view of a specified Government department or other body applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such a requirement applies, the applicant must request"

-- src:597 | (3) Where a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company under this Act, the application must—
-- src:598 | (a) include a statement that a request under this section has been made, and
@ref s 56(3)(a) Statement that a request has been made (application for registration) (src:597-598)
GIVEN `a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(3)(a) the application must include a statement that a request under this section has been made` MEANS
    IF `a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company under this Act, the application must"

-- src:597 | (3) Where a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company under this Act, the application must—
-- src:599 | (b) be accompanied by a copy of any response received.
@ref s 56(3)(b) Copy of any response (application for registration) (src:597-599)
GIVEN `a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a response to the request has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(3)(b) the application must be accompanied by a copy of the response received` MEANS
    IF       `a request under this section is made in connection with an application for the registration of a company`
         AND `a response to the request has been received`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a request under this section is made ... the application must ... be accompanied by a copy of any response received" (nothing to attach where no response has been received)

-- src:600 | (4) Where a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name, the notice of the change sent to the registrar must be accompanied by—
-- src:601 | (a) a statement by a director or secretary of the company that a request under this section has been made, and
@ref s 56(4)(a) Statement by a director or secretary (change of name) (src:600-601)
GIVEN `a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(4)(a) the notice of the change must be accompanied by a statement by a director or secretary that a request has been made` MEANS
    IF `a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name, the notice of the change sent to the registrar must be accompanied by"

-- src:600 | (4) Where a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name, the notice of the change sent to the registrar must be accompanied by—
-- src:602 | (b) a copy of any response received.
@ref s 56(4)(b) Copy of any response (change of name) (src:600-602)
GIVEN `a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a response to the request has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(4)(b) the notice of the change must be accompanied by a copy of the response received` MEANS
    IF       `a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name`
         AND `a response to the request has been received`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a request under this section is made in connection with a change in a company's name, the notice of the change sent to the registrar must be accompanied by ... (b) a copy of any response received" (nothing to attach where no response has been received)

-- src:604 | 56A Names suggesting connection with foreign governments etc
-- src:605 | A company must not be registered under this Act by a name that, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, would be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with—
-- src:606 | (a) a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government, or
-- src:607 | (b) an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments).
@ref s 56A Names suggesting connection with foreign governments etc (src:604-607)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name would be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name would be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56A the company may be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF       `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name would be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government`
         OR  `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name would be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not be registered under this Act by a name that, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, would be likely to give the false impression"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a name that in the Secretary of State's opinion would be likely to give the false impression of a connection in (a) or (b)

