-- =========================================================================================================
-- Prohibitions where a company has been required to change a name (ss 57B, 57C)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The six provisions under which a name can be changed on a direction are listed by s 76D(2) in the Act's own words
-- ("section 64, 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B"); ss 57B and 57C list five of them (not s 64) and add an order under s 73.

-- src:624 | (3) In subsection (1)—
-- src:625 | (a) the reference to the name of a company being changed following a direction under a particular section includes a case where a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction;
@ref s 57B(3)(a) A name determined under section 76D counts as changed following a direction (src:624-625)
GIVEN `the company's name has at any time been changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57B(3)(a) the name is treated as changed following a direction` MEANS
    IF       `the company's name has at any time been changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B`
         OR  `a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to the name of a company being changed following a direction under a particular section includes a case where a new name is determined"

-- src:624 | (3) In subsection (1)—
-- src:626 | (b) the reference to the name of a company being changed following an order under section 73 includes a case where a new name is determined for the company under section 73(4) because of its failure to comply with an order.
@ref s 57B(3)(b) A name determined under section 73(4) counts as changed following an order (src:624-626)
GIVEN `the company's name has at any time been changed following an order under section 73` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new name is determined for the company under section 73(4) because of its failure to comply with an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57B(3)(b) the name is treated as changed following an order` MEANS
    IF       `the company's name has at any time been changed following an order under section 73`
         OR  `a new name is determined for the company under section 73(4) because of its failure to comply with an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to the name of a company being changed following an order under section 73 includes a case where a new name is determined"

-- src:623 | (2) But subsection (1) does not prevent the registration of the company by any name approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 57B(2) Names approved by the Secretary of State (src:623-623)
GIVEN `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57B(2) subsection (1) does not prevent registration of the company by the name` MEANS
    IF `the name is approved by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any name approved by the Secretary of State"

-- src:621 | 57B Prohibition on re-registering name following direction
-- src:622 | (1) Where a company’s name has at any time been changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B, or an order under section 73, the company must not subsequently be registered under this Act by the original name or a name that is similar to it.
@ref s 57B(1) Prohibition on re-registering name following direction (src:621-622)
GIVEN `the name is treated as changed following a direction (s 57B(3)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name is treated as changed following an order (s 57B(3)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name is the original name or a name that is similar to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57B(1) the company may be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF `s 57B(2) subsection (1) does not prevent registration of the company by the name` `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says yes: s 57B(2), "But subsection (1) does not prevent the registration of the company by any name approved by the Secretary of State"
    ELSE IF       (    `the name is treated as changed following a direction (s 57B(3)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   OR  `the name is treated as changed following an order (s 57B(3)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
              AND `the name is the original name or a name that is similar to it`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must not subsequently be registered under this Act by the original name or a name that is similar to it"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company’s name has at any time been changed following a direction ... or an order", and only the original name or a similar one

-- src:633 | (4) For the purposes of this section a person has a “relevant relationship” with a company if the person is—
-- src:634 | (a) an officer, or
-- src:635 | (b) a member or former member.
@ref s 57C(4) "relevant relationship" (src:633-635)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member or former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57C(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer of the company` OR `the person is a member or former member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a “relevant relationship” with a company if the person is— (a) an officer, or (b) a member or former member"

-- src:632 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1) it is irrelevant whether the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time.
@ref s 57C(3) Relationships need not have coincided in time (src:632-632)
GIVEN `the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57C(3) it matters whether the relationships coincided in time` MEANS
    IF `the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is irrelevant whether the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is irrelevant whether the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time"

-- src:636 | (5) In subsection (1)—
-- src:637 | (a) the reference to the name of a company being changed following a direction under a particular section includes a case where a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction;
@ref s 57C(5)(a) A name determined under section 76D counts as changed following a direction (src:636-637)
GIVEN `the company has at any time been directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57C(5)(a) the company is treated as directed to change its name` MEANS
    IF       `the company has at any time been directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B to change its name`
         OR  `a new name is determined for the company under section 76D because of its failure to comply with the direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to the name of a company being changed following a direction under a particular section includes a case where a new name is determined"

