-- src:627 | 57C Name that another company has been directed to change
-- src:628 | (1) Where a company has at any time been directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B, or ordered under section 73, to change its name, no other company may be registered under this Act by that name or a name that is similar if—
-- src:629 | (a) that company is an existing company and there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies, or
-- src:630 | (b) an application has been made for the registration of that company and, if it is registered, there will on its incorporation be a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies.
@ref s 57C(1) Name that another company has been directed to change (src:627-630)
GIVEN `the company is treated as directed to change its name (s 57C(5)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is treated as ordered to change its name (s 57C(5)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name is that name or a name that is similar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that company is an existing company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made for the registration of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has, or has had, a relevant relationship (s 57C(4)) with both companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if that company is registered there will on its incorporation be a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship (s 57C(4)) with both companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57C(1) the other company may be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF `s 57C(2) subsection (1) does not prevent registration of the company by the name` `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says yes: s 57C(2), "But subsection (1) does not prevent the registration of the company by any name approved by the Secretary of State"
    ELSE IF       (    `the company is treated as directed to change its name (s 57C(5)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   OR  `the company is treated as ordered to change its name (s 57C(5)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
              AND `the name is that name or a name that is similar`
              AND (    (    `that company is an existing company`
                        AND `a person has, or has had, a relevant relationship (s 57C(4)) with both companies`)
                   OR  (    `an application has been made for the registration of that company`
                        AND `if that company is registered there will on its incorporation be a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship (s 57C(4)) with both companies`))
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no other company may be registered under this Act by that name or a name that is similar if"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only the cases in (a) and (b), and only that name or a similar one
